{"title":"Tool library borrowing stock","genre":"analysis","brief":"Complete the following real project in the current, initially empty directory. Choose the deliverables, media, tools, structure and implementation that serve the intended user. Build usable artifacts and check your work. Deliver the project itself. Omit personally identifying credits, author signatures and model or toolchain identity labels. No network access or credentials are provided.\n\nA tool library has $180 to buy extra hand tools before spring and wants to reduce unfilled reservations. Fictional historical fulfilled/unfilled reservation counts for four months were clamps 22/6, 24/8, 19/5, 25/10; tile cutters 12/3, 10/4, 11/2, 13/5; socket sets 16/2, 18/3, 20/4, 17/3. Current stock is eight clamps, three cutters, and five socket sets. Additional units cost $22, $85, and $48 respectively. For planning, assume each added unit can fill two otherwise unfilled reservations per month, capped by observed unmet demand. Compare feasible purchases and test sensitivity to one extra reservation filled per unit. Start from an empty directory and choose offline deliverables for the volunteer buyer.","works":{"923f1ac2833fb9a5":{"files":[{"name":"Purchase comparison.xlsx","bytes":13493,"sha256":"843b2d07cb4430fb07958e9fa2a1300d93a649132310221e7b8dcca5b80d3562","kind":"sheet","sheet":{"name":"Purchases","rows":[["Spring purchase comparison","","","","","","",""],["All 31 baskets at the supplied $180 budget. Filter the list or sort by a scenario total. Gains cover four months.","","","","","","",""],[],["Purchase quantities and budget","","","","","Four-month gains by monthly rate","",""],["Clamps","Tile cutters","Socket sets","Cost","Left","1 fill/unit","2 fills/unit","3 fills/unit"],["5","0","1","158","22","24","37","40"],["6","0","1","180","0","27","37","40"],["4","0","1","136","44","20","35","40"],["3","0","2","162","18","20","35","40"],["4","1","0","173","7","20","35","40"],["2","1","1","177","3","16","32","45"],["3","0","1","114","66","16","31","39"]]}},{"name":"Spring buying guide.pdf","bytes":3107,"sha256":"33499f9caeeeb9ced710fbd0f8364e047a7f50d6633ba9eee46a3b634ea14ed8","kind":"pdf","preview":"data/release/assets/33499f9caeeeb9ced710fbd0f8364e047a7f50d6633ba9eee46a3b634ea14ed8-page1.jpg"}],"download":"data/release/assets/6e0366ffcc45dd0f35f6e0c297935aa1aeb7d88065119847af6e453c04f0c01b.zip"},"778bdb65c343dd42":{"files":[{"name":"buyer-brief.pdf","bytes":110369,"sha256":"4b1e06ae790867fb1ae5955b0b0330840035dac923be2d0c8d068948a5df1196","kind":"pdf","preview":"data/release/assets/4b1e06ae790867fb1ae5955b0b0330840035dac923be2d0c8d068948a5df1196-page1.jpg"},{"name":"spring-purchase-planner.html","bytes":26107,"sha256":"7e8882adf1436c7c6d4b3ab785991a910712f062aef94a2b1f7a8634fc713738","kind":"text","body":"<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n<meta name=\"color-scheme\" content=\"light\">\n<title>Spring tool purchase planner</title>\n<style>\n  :root {\n    --ink: #192d25;\n    --muted: #4c5d53;\n    --dark: #193e31;\n    --green: #27634e;\n    --paper: #f7f6ef;\n    --white: #fffefa;\n    --line: #d8dfd4;\n    --mint: #e8f1e8;\n    --lime: #dcecab;\n    --focus: #9c510a;\n    font: 100%/1.5 system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif;\n    color: var(--ink);\n    background: var(--paper);\n  }\n  *, *::before, *::after { box-sizing: border-box; }\n  body { margin: 0; }\n  .wrap { width: min(1120px, calc(100% - 64px)); margin-inline: auto; }\n  .mast { background: var(--dark); color: #fff; }\n  .mast .wrap { min-height: 64px; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: 16px; }\n  .identity { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 11px; font-size: .9rem; font-weight: 700; }\n  .mark { display: grid; place-items: center; width: 32px; height: 29px; border: 1px solid #aec4af; color: var(--lime); font: 700 1rem Georgia, serif; border-radius: 4px; }\n  .mast a { color: #fff; font-size: .9rem; padding-block: 12px; text-underline-offset: 4px; }\n  main { padding-block: 34px 52px; }\n  .intro { display: flex; align-items: end; justify-content: space-between; gap: 20px; margin-bottom: 25px; }\n  h1, h2, p { margin: 0; }\n  h1, h2 { font-family: Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif; font-weight: 500; line-height: 1.07; }\n  h1 { font-size: clamp(2.48rem, 5vw, 4.2rem); letter-spacing: -.048em; }\n  h2 { font-size: clamp(1.65rem, 3.4vw, 2.3rem); letter-spacing: -.035em; }\n  .intro p { color: var(--muted); margin-top: 10px; }\n  .budget { background: var(--lime); border: 1px solid #cddc9b; padding: 10px 16px; border-radius: 6px; min-width: 117px; }\n  .budget strong { display: block; font-size: 1.65rem; line-height: 1.12; }\n  .budget span, .eyebrow { font-size: .73rem; font-weight: 750; letter-spacing: .085em; text-transform: uppercase; }\n  .panel { background: var(--white); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 12px; min-width: 0; }\n  .scenarios { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; gap: 14px; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); padding-block: 14px; }\n  .scenarios p { font-weight: 700; }\n  .choices { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px; }\n  button, select, .action {\n    font: inherit; font-size: .875rem; font-weight: 650; min-height: 44px; padding: 9px 13px;\n    border: 1px solid #a4b6a8; border-radius: 6px; color: var(--ink); background: var(--white);\n  }\n  button, select, .action { cursor: pointer; }\n  .action { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; text-decoration: none; }\n  button:hover, select:hover, .action:hover { background: var(--mint); }\n  button[aria-pressed=\"true\"] { color: #fff; background: var(--dark); border-color: var(--dark); }\n  button:active, .action:active { background: var(--lime); color: var(--ink); }\n  :focus-visible { outline: 3px solid var(--focus); outline-offset: 3px; }\n  .mast :focus-visible { outline-color: var(--lime); }\n  .top { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.18fr 1fr; gap: 16px; }\n  .order, .impact { padding: clamp(16px, 3vw, 27px); }\n  .order { border-top: 4px solid var(--green); }\n  .impact { background: var(--mint); border-color: #ceddce; }\n  .eyebrow { color: var(--green); margin-bottom: 8px; }\n  .order-note { color: var(--muted); font-size: .9rem; margin-top: 8px; }\n  .order table { margin-top: 12px; }\n  table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: .875rem; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }\n  th, td { padding: 10px 8px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); text-align: right; }\n  th:first-child, td:first-child { text-align: left; }\n  thead th { color: var(--muted); font-size: .76rem; font-weight: 730; vertical-align: bottom; }\n  .order th:first-child, .order td:first-child { padding-left: 0; }\n  .order th:last-child, .order td:last-child { padding-right: 0; }\n  .order tbody th { font-weight: 650; }\n  .order-total { margin-top: 15px; display: flex; align-items: baseline; justify-content: space-between; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 3px 14px; }\n  .order-total strong { font-size: 1.28rem; }\n  .order-total span { color: var(--muted); font-size: .9rem; }\n  .impact-total { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 10px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-top: 7px; }\n  .impact-total strong { font: 500 clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 3.5rem)/1 Georgia, serif; letter-spacing: -.05em; }\n  .impact-total span { color: var(--muted); font-size: .9rem; }\n  .bars { list-style: none; margin: 12px 0 9px; padding: 0; }\n  .bars li + li { margin-top: 11px; }\n  .bar-label { display: flex; align-items: baseline; justify-content: space-between; gap: 10px; font-size: .87rem; font-weight: 650; }\n  .bar-label span:last-child { font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; white-space: nowrap; }\n  .bar { height: 8px; background: repeating-linear-gradient(135deg, #c6d4c6 0 3px, #dce7da 3px 6px); border-radius: 5px; overflow: hidden; margin-top: 4px; }\n  .bar-fill { height: 100%; background: var(--green); }\n  .impact-caption { color: var(--muted); font-size: .84rem; }\n  .sensitivity { margin-top: 16px; display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 2.25fr); gap: 15px; padding: 17px 20px; align-items: center; border-left: 4px solid #869949; }\n  .sensitivity h2 { font-size: 1.43rem; }\n  .sensitivity p { font-size: .92rem; }\n  .comparison { margin-top: 32px; }\n  .section-head { display: flex; gap: 14px 20px; align-items: end; justify-content: space-between; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-bottom: 13px; }\n  .section-head p { margin-top: 7px; color: var(--muted); font-size: .89rem; }\n  .controls { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px; align-items: center; }\n  .controls label { font-size: .82rem; font-weight: 650; }\n  select { max-width: 100%; }\n  .comparison table th:first-child, .comparison table td:first-child { padding-left: 16px; }\n  .comparison table th:last-child, .comparison table td:last-child { padding-right: 16px; }\n  .comparison thead { background: #f0f3eb; }\n  .comparison thead th:first-child { border-top-left-radius: 11px; }\n  .comparison thead th:last-child { border-top-right-radius: 11px; }\n  .comparison tbody th { font-weight: 650; }\n  .comparison tbody tr.winner { background: #edf4e5; }\n  .comparison tbody tr:hover { background: #f5f7ee; }\n  .comparison td.active { font-weight: 750; color: var(--dark); }\n  .best-label { color: #30533d; font-size: .72rem; font-weight: 720; display: inline-block; margin-left: 4px; }\n  .table-footer { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; padding: 10px 15px; gap: 8px; flex-wrap: wrap; }\n  .table-footer p { font-size: .85rem; color: var(--muted); }\n  .evidence { margin-top: 28px; padding: 0 19px; }\n  summary { min-height: 52px; padding: 14px 0; cursor: pointer; font-weight: 700; }\n  .evidence-content { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.3fr 1fr; gap: 19px; padding-bottom: 21px; }\n  .evidence h3 { margin: 0 0 7px; font-size: 1rem; }\n  .evidence p { font-size: .89rem; color: var(--muted); }\n  .evidence p + p, .formula + p { margin-top: 9px; }\n  .formula { display: block; background: var(--mint); border-radius: 5px; padding: 8px 10px; margin-top: 8px; font-weight: 650; font-size: .87rem; }\n  .history table { margin: 8px 0; }\n  .history th, .history td { padding: 6px 4px; }\n  .history tbody th { font-weight: 650; }\n  .print-only { display: none; }\n  .sr-only { position: absolute; width: 1px; height: 1px; padding: 0; margin: -1px; overflow: hidden; clip-path: inset(50%); white-space: nowrap; border: 0; }\n  @media (max-width: 760px) {\n    .wrap { width: min(580px, calc(100% - 32px)); }\n    .top, .evidence-content { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }\n    .intro { align-items: start; }\n  }\n  @media (max-width: 510px) {\n    main { padding-top: 24px; }\n    .intro { flex-direction: column; gap: 13px; margin-bottom: 17px; }\n    .budget { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 8px; padding: 7px 10px; }\n    .budget strong { font-size: 1.2rem; }\n    .scenarios { align-items: flex-start; flex-direction: column; gap: 7px; }\n    .sensitivity { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 6px; padding: 14px; }\n    .comparison th, .comparison td { padding: 9px 4px; }\n    .comparison table th:first-child, .comparison table td:first-child { padding-left: 8px; }\n    .comparison table th:last-child, .comparison table td:last-child { padding-right: 8px; }\n    .best-label { display: block; margin: 0; }\n  }\n  @page { size: letter; margin: 0.5in; }\n  @media print {\n    :root { background: white; }\n    .mast, main { display: none; }\n    .print-only { display: block; }\n    .brief { color: #192d25; font-size: 10.5pt; line-height: 1.35; }\n    .brief-head { border-top: 7px solid #27634e; border-bottom: 1px solid #b6c4b8; padding: 14px 0 11px; }\n    .brief h1 { font-size: 31pt; }\n    .brief h2 { font-size: 17pt; margin: 0 0 6px; }\n    .brief section { margin-top: 16px; break-inside: avoid; }\n    .brief .eyebrow { font-size: 8.5pt; margin-bottom: 6px; }\n    .brief-head p:last-child { margin-top: 5px; }\n    .brief .print-buy { padding-left: 11px; border-left: 3px solid #27634e; }\n    .brief table { font-size: 10pt; margin: 6px 0; }\n    .brief thead th { font-size: 9pt; }\n    .brief td, .brief th { padding: 5px 7px; }\n    .brief tbody th { font-weight: 650; }\n    .brief .print-note { margin-top: 6px; }\n  }\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<header class=\"mast\">\n  <div class=\"wrap\">\n    <div class=\"identity\"><span class=\"mark\" aria-hidden=\"true\">TL</span> Tool Library</div>\n    <a href=\"buyer-brief.pdf\">Buyer brief (PDF)</a>\n  </div>\n</header>\n<main class=\"wrap\">\n  <div class=\"intro\">\n    <div>\n      <h1>Spring tool purchase</h1>\n      <p>Choose which extra tools could fill the most reservations.</p>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"budget\"><strong>$180</strong><span>Budget</span></div>\n  </div>\n  <noscript><p>The interactive comparison requires JavaScript. Open the buyer brief linked above for the purchase decision and supporting data.</p></noscript>\n  <div id=\"planner\" hidden>\n    <div class=\"scenarios\">\n      <p id=\"scenario-label\">Reservations each added unit can fill per month</p>\n      <div class=\"choices\" role=\"group\" aria-labelledby=\"scenario-label\">\n        <button type=\"button\" data-rate=\"2\" aria-pressed=\"true\">2 · Base case</button>\n        <button type=\"button\" data-rate=\"3\" aria-pressed=\"false\">3 · Higher capacity</button>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"top\">\n      <section class=\"panel order\" aria-labelledby=\"buy-title\">\n        <p class=\"eyebrow\">Recommended order</p>\n        <h2 id=\"buy-title\"></h2>\n        <p class=\"order-note\" id=\"order-note\"></p>\n        <table aria-label=\"Recommended order and stock after purchase\">\n          <thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Tool</th><th scope=\"col\">Buy</th><th scope=\"col\">Stock after</th><th scope=\"col\">Cost</th></tr></thead>\n          <tbody id=\"order-lines\"></tbody>\n        </table>\n        <p class=\"order-total\"><strong id=\"order-cost\"></strong><span id=\"order-balance\"></span></p>\n      </section>\n\n      <section class=\"panel impact\" aria-labelledby=\"impact-title\">\n        <p class=\"eyebrow\">Four-month estimate</p>\n        <h2 id=\"impact-title\">Reservations recovered</h2>\n        <p class=\"impact-total\"><strong id=\"impact-total\"></strong><span id=\"impact-remaining\"></span></p>\n        <ul class=\"bars\" id=\"impact-bars\" aria-label=\"Recovered reservations by tool\"></ul>\n        <p class=\"impact-caption\">Each bar shows the share of that tool’s observed unmet demand recovered.</p>\n      </section>\n    </div>\n    <p class=\"sr-only\" aria-live=\"polite\" id=\"scenario-status\"></p>\n\n    <section class=\"panel sensitivity\" aria-labelledby=\"sensitivity-title\">\n      <h2 id=\"sensitivity-title\">When capacity rises</h2>\n      <p id=\"sensitivity-copy\"></p>\n    </section>\n\n    <section class=\"comparison\" aria-labelledby=\"compare-title\">\n      <div class=\"section-head\">\n        <div>\n          <h2 id=\"compare-title\">Compare feasible purchases</h2>\n          <p>Reservations recovered across all four months. Impact ties favor lower cost.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"controls\">\n          <label for=\"ranking\">Sort by</label>\n          <select id=\"ranking\">\n            <option value=\"2\">Base-case recovery</option>\n            <option value=\"3\">Higher-capacity recovery</option>\n            <option value=\"cost\">Lowest cost</option>\n          </select>\n          <button type=\"button\" id=\"csv\">Download CSV</button>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"panel\">\n        <table aria-labelledby=\"compare-title\">\n          <thead>\n            <tr>\n              <th scope=\"col\">Clamps</th>\n              <th scope=\"col\" aria-label=\"Tile cutters\">Cutters</th>\n              <th scope=\"col\" aria-label=\"Socket sets\">Socket sets</th>\n              <th scope=\"col\" id=\"cost-head\">Cost</th>\n              <th scope=\"col\" id=\"base-head\" aria-label=\"Recovered at two per added unit per month\">2/unit</th>\n              <th scope=\"col\" id=\"high-head\" aria-label=\"Recovered at three per added unit per month\">3/unit</th>\n            </tr>\n          </thead>\n          <tbody id=\"comparison-lines\"></tbody>\n        </table>\n        <div class=\"table-footer\">\n          <p id=\"row-count\" aria-live=\"polite\"></p>\n          <button type=\"button\" id=\"expand\" aria-controls=\"comparison-lines\" aria-expanded=\"false\"></button>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </section>\n\n    <details class=\"panel evidence\">\n      <summary>Reservation history and calculation</summary>\n      <div class=\"evidence-content\">\n        <section class=\"history\" aria-labelledby=\"history-title\">\n          <h3 id=\"history-title\">Fictional reservation history</h3>\n          <p>Cells show fulfilled / unfilled reservations. Months are in the order supplied.</p>\n          <table aria-labelledby=\"history-title\">\n            <thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Tool</th><th scope=\"col\">M1</th><th scope=\"col\">M2</th><th scope=\"col\">M3</th><th scope=\"col\">M4</th><th scope=\"col\">Total</th></tr></thead>\n            <tbody id=\"history-lines\"></tbody>\n          </table>\n          <p id=\"inputs\"></p>\n        </section>\n        <section aria-labelledby=\"method-title\">\n          <h3 id=\"method-title\">How the estimate works</h3>\n          <p>For each tool and each month, take the smaller of observed unfilled reservations and the added units’ monthly capacity.</p>\n          <span class=\"formula\">Recovered = min(unfilled, added units × monthly rate)</span>\n          <p>Sum those values across all tools and months. Each order uses whole units and costs $180 or less, including the option to buy nothing.</p>\n          <p>The estimate uses the four historical months as a demand proxy for spring. The budget covers the listed unit prices.</p>\n        </section>\n      </div>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n</main>\n\n<article class=\"print-only brief\" aria-label=\"Spring tool purchase buyer brief\">\n  <header class=\"brief-head\">\n    <p class=\"eyebrow\">Tool Library · Buyer brief</p>\n    <h1>Spring tool purchase</h1>\n    <p>$180 budget · Four months of fictional reservation history</p>\n  </header>\n  <section class=\"print-buy\">\n    <h2 id=\"print-buy-title\"></h2>\n    <p id=\"print-buy-copy\"></p>\n    <p class=\"print-note\" id=\"print-stock\"></p>\n  </section>\n  <section>\n    <h2>Compare the leading orders</h2>\n    <table aria-label=\"Leading orders and reservations recovered\">\n      <thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Order</th><th scope=\"col\">Cost</th><th scope=\"col\">At 2/unit</th><th scope=\"col\">At 3/unit</th></tr></thead>\n      <tbody id=\"print-options\"></tbody>\n    </table>\n    <p id=\"print-sensitivity\"></p>\n  </section>\n  <section>\n    <h2>Reservation history</h2>\n    <p>Each cell shows fulfilled / unfilled reservations.</p>\n    <table aria-label=\"Fictional reservation history\">\n      <thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Tool</th><th scope=\"col\">Stock</th><th scope=\"col\">Unit cost</th><th scope=\"col\">M1</th><th scope=\"col\">M2</th><th scope=\"col\">M3</th><th scope=\"col\">M4</th><th scope=\"col\">Total</th></tr></thead>\n      <tbody id=\"print-history\"></tbody>\n    </table>\n  </section>\n  <section>\n    <h2>How the estimate works</h2>\n    <p>For each tool and month, count the smaller of observed unmet demand and added units × monthly capacity. Sum across all tools and months. Compare every whole-unit order within $180 and favor the lower price when recovery is tied.</p>\n    <p class=\"print-note\" id=\"print-method\"></p>\n  </section>\n</article>\n\n<script>\n\"use strict\";\n\nconst budget = 180;\nconst tools = [\n  { name: \"Clamps\", unit: \"clamp\", stock: 8, cost: 22, history: [[22, 6], [24, 8], [19, 5], [25, 10]] },\n  { name: \"Tile cutters\", unit: \"tile cutter\", stock: 3, cost: 85, history: [[12, 3], [10, 4], [11, 2], [13, 5]] },\n  { name: \"Socket sets\", unit: \"socket set\", stock: 5, cost: 48, history: [[16, 2], [18, 3], [20, 4], [17, 3]] },\n];\nconst rates = [2, 3];\nconst sum = values => values.reduce((total, value) => total + value, 0);\nconst unmet = tools.map(tool => sum(tool.history.map(([, unfilled]) => unfilled)));\nconst totalUnmet = sum(unmet);\nconst money = amount => `$${amount}`;\nconst byId = id => document.getElementById(id);\nconst describeOrder = quantities => {\n  const items = quantities.flatMap((quantity, i) => quantity\n    ? [`${quantity} ${quantity === 1 ? tools[i].unit : tools[i].name.toLowerCase()}`]\n    : []);\n  return items.join(\" + \") || \"Buy nothing\";\n};\nconst compareCost = (a, b) => a.cost - b.cost;\nconst compareRecovery = rate => (a, b) => b.recovery[rate].total - a.recovery[rate].total || compareCost(a, b);\n\nfunction enumerateOrders(index = 0, remaining = budget, quantities = []) {\n  if (index === tools.length) {\n    const recovery = Object.fromEntries(rates.map(rate => {\n      const perTool = tools.map((tool, i) => sum(\n        tool.history.map(([, unfilled]) => Math.min(unfilled, quantities[i] * rate))\n      ));\n      return [rate, { total: sum(perTool), perTool }];\n    }));\n    return [{ quantities, cost: budget - remaining, recovery }];\n  }\n\n  const orders = [];\n  const unitCost = tools[index].cost;\n  for (let quantity = 0; quantity * unitCost <= remaining; quantity += 1) {\n    orders.push(...enumerateOrders(index + 1, remaining - quantity * unitCost, [...quantities, quantity]));\n  }\n  return orders;\n}\n\nconst orders = enumerateOrders();\nconst rankings = Object.fromEntries(rates.map(rate => [rate, [...orders].sort(compareRecovery(rate))]));\nrankings.cost = [...orders].sort(compareCost);\nconst base = rankings[2][0];\nconst higher = rankings[3][0];\nconst baseTies = rankings[2].filter(order => order.recovery[2].total === base.recovery[2].total);\nconst showCount = 8;\nlet rate = 2;\nlet sort = \"2\";\nlet expanded = false;\n\nfunction renderScenario() {\n  const best = rankings[rate][0];\n  const impact = best.recovery[rate];\n  const name = describeOrder(best.quantities);\n  byId(\"buy-title\").textContent = name;\n  byId(\"order-note\").textContent = rate === 2\n    ? \"A sixth clamp would use the last $22 and fill zero additional reservations.\"\n    : \"Highest recovery if each added unit can fill three reservations per month.\";\n  byId(\"order-lines\").innerHTML = tools.map((tool, i) => {\n    const added = best.quantities[i];\n    return `<tr><th scope=\"row\">${tool.name}</th><td>${added}</td><td>${tool.stock + added}</td><td>${money(added * tool.cost)}</td></tr>`;\n  }).join(\"\");\n  byId(\"order-cost\").textContent = `${money(best.cost)} total`;\n  byId(\"order-balance\").textContent = `${money(budget - best.cost)} left in budget`;\n  byId(\"impact-total\").textContent = `${impact.total} of ${totalUnmet}`;\n  byId(\"impact-remaining\").textContent = `${totalUnmet - impact.total} still unfilled`;\n  byId(\"impact-bars\").innerHTML = tools.map((tool, i) => `\n    <li>\n      <div class=\"bar-label\"><span>${tool.name}</span><span>${impact.perTool[i]} / ${unmet[i]}</span></div>\n      <div class=\"bar\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><div class=\"bar-fill\" style=\"width:${100 * impact.perTool[i] / unmet[i]}%\"></div></div>\n    </li>`).join(\"\");\n  byId(\"scenario-status\").textContent = `${rate} per unit per month. ${name}. ${money(best.cost)}. ${impact.total} reservations recovered.`;\n\n  document.querySelectorAll(\"[data-rate]\").forEach(button => {\n    button.setAttribute(\"aria-pressed\", String(Number(button.dataset.rate) === rate));\n  });\n}\n\nfunction renderComparison() {\n  const ranked = rankings[sort];\n  const visible = expanded ? ranked : ranked.slice(0, showCount);\n  byId(\"comparison-lines\").innerHTML = visible.map(order => {\n    const best = order === rankings[rate][0];\n    const label = best ? '<span class=\"best-label\">Best</span>' : \"\";\n    const [clamps, cutters, sockets] = order.quantities;\n    return `<tr${best ? ' class=\"winner\"' : \"\"}>\n      <td>${clamps}</td><td>${cutters}</td><td>${sockets}</td>\n      <td>${money(order.cost)}</td>\n      <td${rate === 2 ? ' class=\"active\"' : \"\"}>${order.recovery[2].total}${rate === 2 ? label : \"\"}</td>\n      <td${rate === 3 ? ' class=\"active\"' : \"\"}>${order.recovery[3].total}${rate === 3 ? label : \"\"}</td>\n    </tr>`;\n  }).join(\"\");\n  for (const [value, id] of [[\"cost\", \"cost-head\"], [\"2\", \"base-head\"], [\"3\", \"high-head\"]]) {\n    const head = byId(id);\n    if (value === sort) head.setAttribute(\"aria-sort\", value === \"cost\" ? \"ascending\" : \"descending\");\n    else head.removeAttribute(\"aria-sort\");\n  }\n  byId(\"ranking\").value = sort;\n  byId(\"row-count\").textContent = `Showing ${visible.length} of ${orders.length} orders`;\n  byId(\"expand\").textContent = expanded ? \"Show fewer\" : `Show all ${orders.length} orders`;\n  byId(\"expand\").setAttribute(\"aria-expanded\", String(expanded));\n}\n\nfunction renderHistory() {\n  function historyRows(withStock) {\n    return tools.map((tool, i) => {\n      const totalFulfilled = sum(tool.history.map(([fulfilled]) => fulfilled));\n      const stock = withStock ? `<td>${tool.stock}</td><td>${money(tool.cost)}</td>` : \"\";\n      const months = tool.history.map(([fulfilled, unfilled]) => `<td>${fulfilled}/${unfilled}</td>`).join(\"\");\n      return `<tr><th scope=\"row\">${tool.name}</th>${stock}${months}<td>${totalFulfilled}/${unmet[i]}</td></tr>`;\n    }).join(\"\");\n  }\n  byId(\"history-lines\").innerHTML = historyRows(false);\n  byId(\"print-history\").innerHTML = historyRows(true);\n  byId(\"inputs\").textContent = \"Current stock and unit cost: \" + tools\n    .map(tool => `${tool.name.toLowerCase()} ${tool.stock} at ${money(tool.cost)} each`).join(\" · \");\n}\n\nfunction renderBrief() {\n  const tied = baseTies[1];\n  const cheaper = rankings[2].find(order => order.recovery[2].total < base.recovery[2].total);\n  const noPurchase = rankings.cost[0];\n  const baseRecovered = base.recovery[2].total;\n  const higherRecovered = higher.recovery[3].total;\n  byId(\"sensitivity-copy\").innerHTML = `At 3 per unit per month, <strong>${describeOrder(higher.quantities)}</strong> leads with <strong>${higherRecovered} recovered for ${money(higher.cost)}</strong>. The base-case order recovers ${base.recovery[3].total} at that rate. At 2 per unit, the higher-capacity order recovers ${higher.recovery[2].total}.`;\n  byId(\"print-buy-title\").textContent = `Buy ${describeOrder(base.quantities)} for ${money(base.cost)}`;\n  byId(\"print-buy-copy\").textContent = `At two reservations per added unit per month, this order recovers ${baseRecovered} of ${totalUnmet} across four months, leaving ${totalUnmet - baseRecovered} unfilled and ${money(budget - base.cost)} in the budget. An extra clamp would use the remaining ${money(budget - base.cost)} and recover zero more reservations.`;\n  byId(\"print-stock\").textContent = \"Stock after purchase: \" + tools.map((tool, i) =>\n    `${tool.stock + base.quantities[i]} ${tool.name.toLowerCase()}`).join(\" · \");\n  byId(\"print-options\").innerHTML = [base, tied, cheaper, higher, noPurchase].map(order =>\n    `<tr><th scope=\"row\">${describeOrder(order.quantities)}</th><td>${money(order.cost)}</td><td>${order.recovery[2].total}</td><td>${order.recovery[3].total}</td></tr>`\n  ).join(\"\");\n  byId(\"print-sensitivity\").textContent = `At three per unit per month, ${describeOrder(higher.quantities)} leads at ${higherRecovered} recovered, leaving ${totalUnmet - higherRecovered} unfilled. It costs ${money(higher.cost - base.cost)} more than the base-case order and recovers ${higherRecovered - base.recovery[3].total} more at this rate.`;\n  byId(\"print-method\").textContent = `The ${orders.length} feasible orders include buying nothing. The four historical months serve as a demand proxy for spring. The companion planner lists every order and exports the comparison.`;\n}\n\nfunction downloadComparison() {\n  const header = [\n    \"Clamps added\", \"Tile cutters added\", \"Socket sets added\", \"Cost ($)\", \"Budget left ($)\",\n    \"Recovered at 2 per unit per month\", \"Still unfilled at 2 per unit per month\",\n    \"Recovered at 3 per unit per month\", \"Still unfilled at 3 per unit per month\",\n  ];\n  const rows = rankings[sort].map(order => [\n    ...order.quantities, order.cost, budget - order.cost,\n    ...rates.flatMap(capacity => [order.recovery[capacity].total, totalUnmet - order.recovery[capacity].total]),\n  ]);\n  const csv = [header, ...rows].map(row => row.join(\",\")).join(\"\\r\\n\") + \"\\r\\n\";\n  const url = URL.createObjectURL(new Blob([csv], { type: \"text/csv;charset=utf-8\" }));\n  const link = document.createElement(\"a\");\n  link.href = url;\n  link.download = \"spring-purchase-options.csv\";\n  document.body.append(link);\n  link.click();\n  link.remove();\n  setTimeout(() => URL.revokeObjectURL(url), 1000);\n}\n\ndocument.querySelectorAll(\"[data-rate]\").forEach(button => button.addEventListener(\"click\", () => {\n  rate = Number(button.dataset.rate);\n  sort = String(rate);\n  renderScenario();\n  renderComparison();\n}));\nbyId(\"ranking\").addEventListener(\"change\", event => {\n  sort = event.target.value;\n  renderComparison();\n});\nbyId(\"expand\").addEventListener(\"click\", () => {\n  expanded = !expanded;\n  renderComparison();\n});\nbyId(\"csv\").addEventListener(\"click\", downloadComparison);\n\nrenderScenario();\nrenderComparison();\nrenderHistory();\nrenderBrief();\nbyId(\"planner\").hidden = false;\n</script>\n</body>\n</html>\n"}],"download":"data/release/assets/71cf638f7c4690808269fd3e21b1f7849ea563d20fb2896f8d725631d0ef6df8.zip"